1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,080
I'm Hirotika Nakagawa, and I transferred from Tokyo.

2
00:00:10,460 --> 00:00:11,240
Nice to meet you.

3
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:13,540
Ha! More Tokyo scum!

4
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:18,060
Oh, Hirotika.

5
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:19,100
Kuya?

6
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:20,920
Kuya, is that you?

7
00:00:21,320 --> 00:00:24,200
It was a fateful reunion.

8
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:27,740
Rika thinks it looks perfect!

9
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:28,500
I agree.

10
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:30,380
Okay, we got it, guys.

11
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:32,740
Let's start getting ready for the next scene.

12
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:35,500
Everybody good to go?

13
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:36,820
I'm all set here.

14
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:38,400
Jeez, this is heavy.

15
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:42,300
Okay, lights, camera, action!

16
00:00:44,160 --> 00:00:46,120
You've got some nerve, you know that!

17
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:48,240
What? Why, how dare you?

18
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:49,920
How dare I? How dare you?

19
00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:50,840
Awesome, cut!

20
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:52,720
Now, what's after this scene?

21
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:55,660
Hey, Yozara?

22
00:00:56,380 --> 00:00:56,620
Huh?

23
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:59,380
The sun is setting, so we're losing our light.

24
00:00:59,740 --> 00:01:01,960
Anything we shoot now won't match the other footage.

25
00:01:02,540 --> 00:01:02,980
Hmm.

26
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:04,680
Well, that's that, then.

27
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:06,120
Hey, guys!

28
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:07,440
We'll pick it up tomorrow.

29
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:09,020
Meet in the clubroom after school.

30
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:12,040
We're running a little behind, so do not be late.

31
00:01:12,180 --> 00:01:12,700
Okay.

32
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:15,100
I can't hear you!

33
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:15,600
Okay!

34
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:15,740
Okay!

35
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:16,500
Yeah!

36
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:16,700
Yeah!

37
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:46,680
Thank you.

38
00:02:46,875 --> 00:02:58,115
No scenes with Kotaro today either.

39
00:02:59,115 --> 00:03:01,315
Man, I wish I had a little more screen time.

40
00:03:01,915 --> 00:03:04,455
But being a part of the crew is more fun than I thought it'd be,

41
00:03:04,535 --> 00:03:05,575
so I guess it's all right.

42
00:03:08,855 --> 00:03:11,035
Those must be the score rankings from finals.

43
00:03:16,875 --> 00:03:19,535
Senna scored 895 out of 900.

44
00:03:19,615 --> 00:03:22,115
I didn't know someone could even get a score that high.

45
00:03:24,255 --> 00:03:26,955
Yozura got the highest score in our class, too.

46
00:03:29,715 --> 00:03:30,955
What's that about?

47
00:03:31,955 --> 00:03:32,955
Gross.

48
00:03:34,635 --> 00:03:36,455
Hey, you got some kind of problem, pal?

49
00:03:36,535 --> 00:03:39,295
What? I don't think so. No problem here.

50
00:03:39,395 --> 00:03:42,395
Hold on. You're Senna Kashiwazaki's boyfriend, aren't you?

51
00:03:42,475 --> 00:03:43,395
I, huh?

52
00:03:43,475 --> 00:03:44,995
I know it's true.

53
00:03:45,075 --> 00:03:46,635
Curse that tricky Senna.

54
00:03:46,635 --> 00:03:49,175
If a mortal enemy is a thing, she's totally mine.

55
00:03:49,295 --> 00:03:50,175
I'm getting that.

56
00:03:50,295 --> 00:03:52,075
So no offense, but who are you anyway?

57
00:03:52,635 --> 00:03:55,175
Are you serious? You really don't know who I am?

58
00:03:55,315 --> 00:03:56,135
Good grief.

59
00:03:56,455 --> 00:03:58,855
I suppose I should have expected an associate of Senna's

60
00:03:58,855 --> 00:03:59,975
to be as rude as she is.

61
00:03:59,975 --> 00:04:02,575
Wow. Okay. Are you, like, famous or something?

62
00:04:02,815 --> 00:04:03,355
Should be.

63
00:04:03,475 --> 00:04:05,955
My name's Awa Yusef, student council treasurer,

64
00:04:06,415 --> 00:04:08,335
year two, class three, ranked second.

65
00:04:08,775 --> 00:04:09,135
Oh.

66
00:04:10,415 --> 00:04:11,515
Class three, huh?

67
00:04:11,795 --> 00:04:12,975
That's Senna's class.

68
00:04:13,455 --> 00:04:16,195
You're in the student council and ranked second in our whole grade?

69
00:04:16,195 --> 00:04:17,195
That's impressive.

70
00:04:17,195 --> 00:04:20,735
Your condescending attitude is more than a little obnoxious.

71
00:04:20,735 --> 00:04:24,735
I don't need you to remind me I've been Senna Kashiwazaki's runner-up since last year.

72
00:04:24,735 --> 00:04:28,735
I don't know anything about last year, but this year it looks like you're doing really great.

73
00:04:28,735 --> 00:04:29,735
Senna is just tough, that's all.

74
00:04:29,735 --> 00:04:30,735
Shut up.

75
00:04:30,735 --> 00:04:36,135
So what? I want to win by getting better exam scores, if nothing else.

76
00:04:36,535 --> 00:04:41,215
She's the most glamorous, gets the highest grades ever, and is one of the best athletes at school.

77
00:04:41,555 --> 00:04:43,535
Not to mention she's a rich little princess.

78
00:04:43,535 --> 00:04:47,415
I feel like I've heard all this somewhere before.

79
00:04:47,495 --> 00:04:48,735
That's not the worst part.

80
00:04:49,055 --> 00:04:52,275
I know for a fact she's one of those people with so-called real lives.

81
00:04:52,355 --> 00:04:54,495
Now, on top of that, she's got a boyfriend?

82
00:04:54,835 --> 00:04:56,695
No one person is supposed to get that much.

83
00:04:56,815 --> 00:04:58,295
Her existence is a mockery.

84
00:04:58,695 --> 00:05:00,975
It's not fair, Senna's boyfriend. It's not.

85
00:05:01,035 --> 00:05:02,095
Slow down a second.

86
00:05:02,195 --> 00:05:04,535
I am not now, nor have I ever dated Senna.

87
00:05:04,535 --> 00:05:06,935
Oh, please, don't try to lie to me.

88
00:05:07,135 --> 00:05:11,435
You forget. I've seen the two of you together, and there's obviously something going on there.

89
00:05:11,555 --> 00:05:16,295
The other guys in school can barely even talk to her, yet you have no problem chatting her up left and right.

90
00:05:16,535 --> 00:05:18,655
This chick is not what I'd call a listener.

91
00:05:19,155 --> 00:05:22,575
I mean, jeez. I'm fighting like hell to get a higher score than her.

92
00:05:22,735 --> 00:05:25,575
Meanwhile, she goes out and gets herself a super cool boyfriend.

93
00:05:25,795 --> 00:05:27,255
Like I said, it isn't fair!

94
00:05:28,555 --> 00:05:29,695
A moment, please.

95
00:05:29,895 --> 00:05:32,055
You just referred to her boyfriend as cool.

96
00:05:32,575 --> 00:05:33,855
Are you talking about me?

97
00:05:33,855 --> 00:05:36,275
Uh, do you see anyone else standing there?

98
00:05:36,455 --> 00:05:39,175
I mean, it doesn't matter how you look at it. You're super cool.

99
00:05:39,535 --> 00:05:42,815
There's that natural-looking blonde hair you obviously dye regularly.

100
00:05:43,095 --> 00:05:45,715
And you wear your pants rolled up like the hipster you are.

101
00:05:46,375 --> 00:05:47,795
Some might call it fashion.

102
00:05:48,075 --> 00:05:52,935
The point is, you're clearly another one of those special having-life people because you're so damn cool.

103
00:05:54,755 --> 00:05:57,495
Thank you. Nobody's ever talked to me like that before.

104
00:05:57,495 --> 00:06:00,235
Why are you making that stupid face? Come on!

105
00:06:00,435 --> 00:06:03,135
Great, so on top of being cool, you also have a sense of humor.

106
00:06:03,135 --> 00:06:05,975
I can't help but be impressed, but I hate it so much.

107
00:06:06,055 --> 00:06:07,935
Fine, you win. I'm jealous of both of you.

108
00:06:08,055 --> 00:06:11,755
Mr. Perfect and Little Miss Perfect are perfect, perfect, perfect for each other.

109
00:06:11,975 --> 00:06:13,335
Vomit. I'm so out of here.

110
00:06:13,335 --> 00:06:20,175
So that's Aoi Yusa.

111
00:06:20,175 --> 00:06:24,215
Apparently, this place is freaking packed with weirdos.

112
00:06:24,215 --> 00:06:30,775
Yo, what's up?

113
00:06:30,775 --> 00:06:33,575
Hey, why are you the only one here?

114
00:06:33,935 --> 00:06:36,995
Yozora and Rika left to go scout out a new location for filming.

115
00:06:37,395 --> 00:06:39,855
Something about a shot of the sun setting into the sea.

116
00:06:40,095 --> 00:06:45,875
Uh, hey, on the way here, I ran into a girl named Aoi Yusa checking out the finals rankings.

117
00:06:45,915 --> 00:06:46,955
Who is that person?

118
00:06:47,175 --> 00:06:50,155
You mean you don't already know her? She's in your class.

119
00:06:50,155 --> 00:06:50,995
What?

120
00:06:50,995 --> 00:06:54,275
She's kind of short and has this shortish-reddish hair thing going on.

121
00:06:54,275 --> 00:06:57,695
Oh, yeah. Short and shortish-reddish kind of rings a bell.

122
00:06:57,995 --> 00:07:00,655
You should know the people you're in class with, at least.

123
00:07:00,775 --> 00:07:03,655
Well, I memorized all the names of the girls who sit close to me.

124
00:07:03,955 --> 00:07:05,635
Not that it ever paid off any.

125
00:07:05,755 --> 00:07:07,015
What? Did something happen?

126
00:07:07,255 --> 00:07:08,215
I told you.

127
00:07:08,755 --> 00:07:11,215
There are only two types of girls in this world.

128
00:07:11,855 --> 00:07:16,115
Awesome girls, the kind I can be friends with, and all those other bitches.

129
00:07:16,975 --> 00:07:20,435
Besides, why should I be forced to learn a bunch of mongrels' names?

130
00:07:20,435 --> 00:07:21,255
Why? Don't come.

131
00:07:21,695 --> 00:07:23,815
She calls the people in her class mongrels?

132
00:07:24,115 --> 00:07:30,135
Well, evidently this Aoi girl isn't very happy that she's always listed right below you on every single test ranking.

133
00:07:30,335 --> 00:07:32,555
Why would I care about another student's rank?

134
00:07:32,835 --> 00:07:35,275
Did you see the scores? Where are those things even posted?

135
00:07:35,395 --> 00:07:36,915
On the bulletin board in the courtyard.

136
00:07:37,495 --> 00:07:39,015
Oh, guess that makes sense.

137
00:07:39,075 --> 00:07:40,015
You mean you never looked?

138
00:07:40,555 --> 00:07:44,875
I don't have to. I can tell my rank from the paper that has our percentiles and stuff on it.

139
00:07:44,955 --> 00:07:47,595
The only thing that matters to me is that I come in first.

140
00:07:47,715 --> 00:07:48,855
You really are something.

141
00:07:49,335 --> 00:07:50,075
Yeah, thank you.

142
00:07:50,075 --> 00:07:54,055
What kind of studying do you normally do for your classes? Please tell me you have a tutor.

143
00:07:54,375 --> 00:07:56,955
No way. I don't study outside of school and homework.

144
00:07:57,215 --> 00:07:59,615
You're kidding me. You study for tests, though, right?

145
00:07:59,815 --> 00:08:02,095
Not besides that one time we studied together.

146
00:08:02,335 --> 00:08:04,715
But hey, that was a pretty good time, though, wasn't it?

147
00:08:04,715 --> 00:08:07,335
Oh, yeah. Yeah, I guess it was.

148
00:08:07,415 --> 00:08:08,495
So what's the deal?

149
00:08:09,455 --> 00:08:11,635
Did something weird happen with that Aoi girl?

150
00:08:12,055 --> 00:08:13,475
Meh. Never mind.

151
00:08:13,755 --> 00:08:14,195
Okay.

152
00:08:14,915 --> 00:08:15,675
It's weird.

153
00:08:15,975 --> 00:08:19,335
She honestly couldn't care less about anything that doesn't affect her directly.

154
00:08:19,335 --> 00:08:23,915
Yet when she does care about something, she gets so into it, she makes it awkward.

155
00:08:23,915 --> 00:08:28,875
When it comes to Yozara, even if she doesn't like it, she gets practically criminal.

156
00:08:29,835 --> 00:08:31,475
The photos might be criminal.

157
00:08:32,335 --> 00:08:35,415
She lives for what makes her happy and does exactly what she wants.

158
00:08:35,975 --> 00:08:40,595
Doesn't help that she's got a crazy amount of talent and a rich enough family to get away with it all, too.

159
00:08:41,295 --> 00:08:42,515
She's a born princess.

160
00:08:42,515 --> 00:08:46,335
Maybe it's only natural for all the girls in the world to hate her.

161
00:08:47,475 --> 00:08:52,735
Now that I think about it, getting to hang out with her probably is some sort of bizarre divine honor.

162
00:08:54,735 --> 00:08:57,115
We found the perfect location, you guys!

163
00:08:57,235 --> 00:08:58,735
But we have to go there right now.

164
00:08:59,415 --> 00:09:00,455
Game over, neat.

165
00:09:00,655 --> 00:09:01,075
Hey!

166
00:09:01,555 --> 00:09:03,335
Why are you still sitting? Let's go!

167
00:09:03,615 --> 00:09:04,635
Yeah, okay.

168
00:09:04,855 --> 00:09:08,015
And... action!

169
00:09:08,015 --> 00:09:11,235
Get ready, Herotica, because I'm coming strong.

170
00:09:14,235 --> 00:09:16,175
Kuya, what is wrong with you?

171
00:09:16,655 --> 00:09:17,095
Cut!

172
00:09:19,915 --> 00:09:21,795
Okay, we're looking pretty good!

173
00:09:21,995 --> 00:09:24,375
Hey, Rika, are you sure this will work out?

174
00:09:24,395 --> 00:09:25,395
Yeah, why would it not?

175
00:09:26,715 --> 00:09:29,395
I don't know, maybe because we're obviously in a park?

176
00:09:29,815 --> 00:09:31,495
There's no need to worry about that.

177
00:09:31,735 --> 00:09:35,135
Rika's going to use CG later to make it appear like the whole scene's at the beach.

178
00:09:35,255 --> 00:09:36,175
It'll be so fun!

179
00:09:36,175 --> 00:09:42,655
Rika needs to go edit this, so she'll see you later!

180
00:09:42,995 --> 00:09:43,715
Okay, bye then.

181
00:09:44,715 --> 00:09:48,295
I wonder if she'll actually be able to make that beach scene thing work.

182
00:09:48,635 --> 00:09:51,075
I mean, she's a scientist, not a CG expert.

183
00:09:51,455 --> 00:09:53,115
Well, if it isn't Kodika!

184
00:09:54,755 --> 00:09:55,895
Oh, hi, President!

185
00:09:56,115 --> 00:09:57,695
Hi! Fancy seeing you here.

186
00:09:57,995 --> 00:09:59,695
Well, we're at school, so...

187
00:09:59,695 --> 00:10:00,075
Right.

188
00:10:01,855 --> 00:10:04,075
Our festival atmosphere is rather pleasant.

189
00:10:04,435 --> 00:10:05,055
Don't you agree?

190
00:10:05,055 --> 00:10:06,895
Yeah, I guess it is.

191
00:10:12,595 --> 00:10:15,855
Now, if I recall correctly, your club is doing a movie, right?

192
00:10:16,055 --> 00:10:16,535
Yes, sir.

193
00:10:16,875 --> 00:10:18,435
I certainly enjoy a good flick.

194
00:10:18,915 --> 00:10:22,415
And believe it or not, your father used to drag me out to the movies all the time.

195
00:10:22,735 --> 00:10:22,875
Ha!

196
00:10:23,375 --> 00:10:23,595
Ha!

197
00:10:23,595 --> 00:10:24,855
What's funny?

198
00:10:25,295 --> 00:10:25,695
Nothing.

199
00:10:25,975 --> 00:10:26,555
Nothing at all.

200
00:10:26,975 --> 00:10:28,535
Tell me about this movie you're making.

201
00:10:28,755 --> 00:10:29,355
What's it like?

202
00:10:29,455 --> 00:10:30,255
Senna didn't say.

203
00:10:30,755 --> 00:10:32,475
Senna hasn't told you what it's about?

204
00:10:32,775 --> 00:10:36,475
Well, I don't have as much time to speak with her as I'd like.

205
00:10:36,895 --> 00:10:37,215
Cool.

206
00:10:37,295 --> 00:10:37,895
I get that.

207
00:10:40,275 --> 00:10:43,075
When you're done, I'd love to watch the movie, if that's okay.

208
00:10:43,075 --> 00:10:43,875
Sorry.

209
00:10:44,035 --> 00:10:46,655
I'd feel a little awkward having someone I know watch it.

210
00:10:46,715 --> 00:10:47,855
By the way, Kodaka?

211
00:10:48,295 --> 00:10:48,655
Yeah?

212
00:10:49,455 --> 00:10:52,715
I'm curious how your relationship with Senna has been coming along.

213
00:10:52,955 --> 00:10:53,235
Huh?

214
00:10:53,495 --> 00:10:55,055
I'm not sure what you mean.

215
00:10:55,295 --> 00:10:56,075
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

216
00:10:56,175 --> 00:10:57,035
I'm a jerk.

217
00:10:57,115 --> 00:10:59,555
Of course you're too embarrassed to talk to me about it.

218
00:10:59,715 --> 00:11:01,035
No, I'm not embarrassed, sir.

219
00:11:01,075 --> 00:11:02,115
It's just that...

220
00:11:02,115 --> 00:11:03,615
What do you mean by...

221
00:11:03,615 --> 00:11:05,215
Our relationship?

222
00:11:05,575 --> 00:11:05,755
Ha!

223
00:11:05,875 --> 00:11:06,875
We're just guys.

224
00:11:06,875 --> 00:11:08,295
You don't have to play dumb with me.

225
00:11:08,335 --> 00:11:09,195
I'm not playing.

226
00:11:09,455 --> 00:11:10,635
Um, I don't...

227
00:11:10,635 --> 00:11:11,915
I'm really confused, sir.

228
00:11:18,375 --> 00:11:21,395
It is my understanding that you and Senna are dating.

229
00:11:21,675 --> 00:11:22,735
Not accurate, sir.

230
00:11:25,395 --> 00:11:25,875
What?

231
00:11:31,535 --> 00:11:32,915
I have to go now.

232
00:11:33,295 --> 00:11:34,095
Sorry, urgent.

233
00:11:34,315 --> 00:11:35,215
See you another day.

234
00:11:35,595 --> 00:11:36,015
Sure.

235
00:11:36,015 --> 00:11:37,015
See you another day.

236
00:11:43,735 --> 00:11:44,975
Damn you, Fade!

237
00:11:45,055 --> 00:11:46,215
What's going on?

238
00:11:49,935 --> 00:11:51,815
Why is everyone so weird?

239
00:11:52,195 --> 00:11:53,295
I don't get it.

240
00:11:58,695 --> 00:11:59,475
Hey, guys.

241
00:11:59,555 --> 00:12:00,055
What's up?

242
00:12:00,595 --> 00:12:02,055
Kodaka, come with me real quick.

243
00:12:03,015 --> 00:12:03,455
Why?

244
00:12:03,855 --> 00:12:05,515
What the hell are you doing, fog lights?

245
00:12:05,515 --> 00:12:06,855
We have to do something.

246
00:12:07,135 --> 00:12:07,935
We'll be right back.

247
00:12:08,395 --> 00:12:09,855
Jeez, Senna, what's your deal?

248
00:12:17,935 --> 00:12:18,935
It's hot.

249
00:12:18,935 --> 00:12:22,355
Yeah, so what are we here for?

250
00:12:22,355 --> 00:12:23,355
I think...

251
00:12:23,355 --> 00:12:27,215
Well, it looks like Daddy thought you and I were dating.

252
00:12:27,215 --> 00:12:28,555
Oh, yeah, I heard.

253
00:12:28,555 --> 00:12:30,515
Oh, yeah, I heard.

254
00:12:32,015 --> 00:12:36,055
Yesterday he asked me if we were in a relationship and seemed upset when I told him no.

255
00:12:36,675 --> 00:12:39,195
Do you have any idea where he got that from?

256
00:12:39,495 --> 00:12:41,775
Well, uh, let me think.

257
00:12:42,175 --> 00:12:43,675
I'm not sure how to put this.

258
00:12:44,055 --> 00:12:46,035
Will you please stop glaring at me first, though?

259
00:12:46,195 --> 00:12:47,435
I'm not glaring at you.

260
00:12:47,495 --> 00:12:48,355
I'm just suspicious.

261
00:12:48,355 --> 00:12:52,235
Okay, um, remember how we all went to the amusement park?

262
00:12:52,435 --> 00:12:53,795
Yeah, I remember.

263
00:12:54,375 --> 00:12:57,135
And, well, I got those tickets from Daddy, right?

264
00:12:57,475 --> 00:12:58,535
So you said.

265
00:13:03,315 --> 00:13:05,355
See, when he gave them to me, I said...

266
00:13:06,235 --> 00:13:07,315
Thank you!

267
00:13:07,695 --> 00:13:10,135
Kobito's for sure gonna be my little sister now!

268
00:13:11,055 --> 00:13:11,495
What?

269
00:13:11,495 --> 00:13:15,335
I think that gave Daddy the wrong idea about you and me and stuff.

270
00:13:15,655 --> 00:13:17,015
You're not making sense.

271
00:13:17,175 --> 00:13:18,855
Jeez, why do you have to be so stupid?

272
00:13:19,035 --> 00:13:19,675
Think about it.

273
00:13:19,695 --> 00:13:20,675
If we got married...

274
00:13:20,675 --> 00:13:23,335
Then that would mean I, um...

275
00:13:23,335 --> 00:13:26,695
If we were married, Kobito would literally be my sister.

276
00:13:26,915 --> 00:13:27,715
If we're what?

277
00:13:28,015 --> 00:13:30,075
I guess that's true, but I'm still lost.

278
00:13:30,095 --> 00:13:33,835
And at the time, I was just so excited, I didn't really think all that much about it.

279
00:13:34,095 --> 00:13:37,455
Now, in hindsight, I remember he was acting all weird.

280
00:13:38,335 --> 00:13:41,475
Like he'd ask, are there plans to make Kobito your official sister?

281
00:13:41,815 --> 00:13:44,195
And how has your relationship been progressing?

282
00:13:44,635 --> 00:13:45,415
It was weird.

283
00:13:45,615 --> 00:13:46,455
Sounds that way.

284
00:13:46,855 --> 00:13:47,995
How did you answer him?

285
00:13:48,255 --> 00:13:49,315
Oh, I've got this.

286
00:13:49,395 --> 00:13:50,215
Don't you worry.

287
00:13:50,675 --> 00:13:51,115
Crap.

288
00:13:52,155 --> 00:13:52,515
What?

289
00:13:52,895 --> 00:13:55,795
So it seems he didn't realize I was talking about Kobito.

290
00:13:56,135 --> 00:13:58,355
He kind of thought I was talking about you and me.

291
00:13:59,895 --> 00:14:01,075
Are you serious?

292
00:14:01,555 --> 00:14:03,935
If it helps, I feel really bad about it.

293
00:14:05,455 --> 00:14:08,835
Well, you cleared all that up and explained everything to him, didn't you?

294
00:14:09,375 --> 00:14:09,815
Yeah.

295
00:14:10,135 --> 00:14:10,815
That's good.

296
00:14:11,495 --> 00:14:15,195
As long as he knows it was just a big misunderstanding, I'm sure it'll be fine.

297
00:14:15,835 --> 00:14:18,855
I kind of feel bad for him, but at least he knows the truth.

298
00:14:19,235 --> 00:14:22,295
So, uh, here's what I wanted to talk about.

299
00:14:22,895 --> 00:14:23,295
What?

300
00:14:23,595 --> 00:14:25,095
There's more going on than that?

301
00:14:25,535 --> 00:14:25,935
Mm-hmm.

302
00:14:26,675 --> 00:14:29,435
But for the record, this is absolutely in no way my fault.

303
00:14:29,475 --> 00:14:30,115
You got that?

304
00:14:30,795 --> 00:14:34,395
Daddy only just told me about this because of the crap drama that's been going on between

305
00:14:34,395 --> 00:14:34,835
us lately.

306
00:14:34,835 --> 00:14:36,135
Oh, okay.

307
00:14:37,455 --> 00:14:42,415
Well, he told me that, um, you and I are kind of engaged.

308
00:14:42,415 --> 00:14:46,015
Are you all right?

309
00:14:46,515 --> 00:14:48,715
Uh, oh, yeah, uh-huh.

310
00:14:48,715 --> 00:14:54,675
Daddy says, back when we were too young to remember, he and your dad made this promise

311
00:14:54,675 --> 00:14:55,315
to each other.

312
00:14:55,315 --> 00:14:58,195
Basically, we're what you'd call betrothed.

313
00:14:58,835 --> 00:14:59,275
Betrothed?

314
00:14:59,275 --> 00:15:01,355
What are we, like a freaking soap opera?

315
00:15:02,175 --> 00:15:06,095
Might as well be, since they also decided they should write up a marriage pact and put

316
00:15:06,095 --> 00:15:07,215
our thumbprints on it.

317
00:15:07,475 --> 00:15:08,835
Have you seen this pact?

318
00:15:08,995 --> 00:15:09,655
I have!

319
00:15:09,935 --> 00:15:11,615
Our little prints are pretty adorable.

320
00:15:11,735 --> 00:15:12,635
They're so tiny.

321
00:15:12,875 --> 00:15:13,155
What?

322
00:15:13,155 --> 00:15:13,775
Really?

323
00:15:14,275 --> 00:15:14,895
That's weird.

324
00:15:15,095 --> 00:15:16,475
I don't remember that at all.

325
00:15:16,675 --> 00:15:18,695
I didn't remember either, but it's true.

326
00:15:18,875 --> 00:15:19,435
Hold on.

327
00:15:19,735 --> 00:15:20,355
Here, look.

328
00:15:21,375 --> 00:15:22,255
It's us.

329
00:15:22,595 --> 00:15:23,075
Yep.

330
00:15:23,535 --> 00:15:26,055
It looks like we met way before we thought we did.

331
00:15:26,595 --> 00:15:27,695
How crazy.

332
00:15:29,455 --> 00:15:30,015
Crazy.

333
00:15:30,315 --> 00:15:31,395
That's the word for it.

334
00:15:32,555 --> 00:15:34,135
I can't believe this.

335
00:15:38,595 --> 00:15:41,275
Well, regardless, it doesn't matter.

336
00:15:41,475 --> 00:15:41,755
Nope.

337
00:15:41,755 --> 00:15:43,955
I mean, it's not like we're going to get married.

338
00:15:44,175 --> 00:15:44,695
No way.

339
00:15:45,235 --> 00:15:48,775
Not to mention the fact that we shouldn't have to worry about an engagement we didn't make.

340
00:15:48,875 --> 00:15:50,095
That would just be silly, right?

341
00:15:51,915 --> 00:15:53,135
Yes, totally right.

342
00:15:53,695 --> 00:15:56,735
Our dads are beyond random, and that stuff has nothing to do with us.

343
00:15:56,935 --> 00:15:57,535
It's funny.

344
00:15:58,035 --> 00:16:02,535
When it comes to my dad, well, knowing him the way I do, I seriously doubt that he remembers

345
00:16:02,535 --> 00:16:03,335
this pact at all.

346
00:16:03,335 --> 00:16:04,055
You think he won't?

347
00:16:04,275 --> 00:16:05,075
Not even a little.

348
00:16:05,255 --> 00:16:07,435
Trust me, there's no reason for us to sweat this thing.

349
00:16:07,775 --> 00:16:09,175
Well, okay, that's good news.

350
00:16:09,175 --> 00:16:10,935
There's no reason for us to sweat it.

351
00:16:10,935 --> 00:16:13,655
Although, that does kind of make me sad.

352
00:16:13,975 --> 00:16:14,235
Huh?

353
00:16:14,655 --> 00:16:15,655
I didn't say anything.

354
00:16:16,435 --> 00:16:18,475
Besides, it doesn't really matter if we're engaged.

355
00:16:18,635 --> 00:16:19,375
I don't need you.

356
00:16:19,475 --> 00:16:21,615
I can make Kobito my sister all by myself.

357
00:16:22,035 --> 00:16:25,015
I don't suppose I can convince you to give up on that, can I?

358
00:16:26,315 --> 00:16:26,755
Whatever.

359
00:16:27,075 --> 00:16:28,255
Let's go back to the club room.

360
00:16:28,255 --> 00:16:35,795
Look, we may be fine, but I'm a little worried that Slozaro will get all pissy when she finds

361
00:16:35,795 --> 00:16:36,515
out about it.

362
00:16:37,815 --> 00:16:40,195
Well, we don't have to tell her about it, do we?

363
00:16:41,035 --> 00:16:42,855
I mean, it doesn't matter anyway.

364
00:16:42,855 --> 00:16:46,495
Yeah, I guess not.

365
00:16:47,775 --> 00:16:48,235
Cool.

366
00:16:48,955 --> 00:16:49,655
Let's go.

367
00:16:53,855 --> 00:16:54,775
You're late!

368
00:16:54,935 --> 00:16:56,555
What took so damn long?

369
00:16:56,975 --> 00:16:58,095
Oh, nothing too important.

370
00:16:58,375 --> 00:17:00,275
So are we gonna go film now or what?

371
00:17:02,515 --> 00:17:03,595
Yes, we are.

372
00:17:04,395 --> 00:17:05,515
Okay, let's roll.

373
00:17:05,515 --> 00:17:07,615
We can start with the baseball field scene.

374
00:17:11,095 --> 00:17:12,835
It's movie making time!

375
00:17:12,935 --> 00:17:13,295
Maria?

376
00:17:13,595 --> 00:17:13,935
What?

377
00:17:14,115 --> 00:17:15,115
I'm just excited.

378
00:17:15,535 --> 00:17:17,735
I like making movies with my big brother.

379
00:17:19,035 --> 00:17:20,955
Movies, movies, movies are not made of...

380
00:17:20,955 --> 00:17:24,015
I have this weird feeling like I'm forgetting something really important.

381
00:17:25,355 --> 00:17:28,315
But you do have Senna, so, well, that's out.

382
00:17:29,095 --> 00:17:29,975
Hold on.

383
00:17:30,275 --> 00:17:33,635
If Kate thought Senna and I were together, I wonder if...

384
00:17:33,635 --> 00:17:34,095
Right.

385
00:17:34,675 --> 00:17:36,735
Are you and Senna really gonna get married?

386
00:17:37,075 --> 00:17:40,075
The stupid hag told me yesterday that you guys were fiancés.

387
00:17:41,095 --> 00:17:43,035
The word is fiancés, right?

388
00:17:43,175 --> 00:17:45,095
I can't believe how grown up you must be.

389
00:17:45,175 --> 00:17:47,835
If you get to have your very own fiancés, you're gonna get married!

390
00:17:49,295 --> 00:17:51,435
Married people are grown-up fiancés!

391
00:17:53,035 --> 00:17:55,555
Um, what is she talking about?

392
00:17:55,555 --> 00:17:56,055
Huh?

393
00:18:03,635 --> 00:18:06,435
They're betrothed.

394
00:18:06,975 --> 00:18:09,855
And they met when they were, like, super little kids.

395
00:18:10,435 --> 00:18:11,735
But it's no biggie.

396
00:18:12,055 --> 00:18:15,015
What happened between our dads back then has nothing to do with us today.

397
00:18:15,395 --> 00:18:16,055
Isn't that right?

398
00:18:16,315 --> 00:18:16,835
That's right.

399
00:18:16,935 --> 00:18:18,075
Yep, that's totally right!

400
00:18:18,815 --> 00:18:20,755
Rika, I have a question.

401
00:18:21,055 --> 00:18:21,855
Yes, Yozara?

402
00:18:22,175 --> 00:18:23,535
How can Rika help you?

403
00:18:23,875 --> 00:18:28,515
Do you think people who are childhood friends or engaged since before they can remember are closer?

404
00:18:28,515 --> 00:18:32,795
Rika believes most people probably believe being betrothed is indeed closer.

405
00:18:33,535 --> 00:18:34,935
That's what I thought.

406
00:18:35,615 --> 00:18:38,755
Although I guess when you think about how long they've known each other,

407
00:18:38,915 --> 00:18:41,335
one could consider them childhood friends as well.

408
00:18:42,095 --> 00:18:43,575
That's what I thought.

409
00:18:43,635 --> 00:18:45,735
Oh, come on! Will you get over it yourself?

410
00:18:46,295 --> 00:18:48,795
We're saying it doesn't matter, so why are you being so dramatic?

411
00:18:49,155 --> 00:18:52,795
If you can't step out of it on your own, let's see how...

412
00:18:52,795 --> 00:18:56,355
Meat, you're going to regret that.

413
00:18:58,515 --> 00:19:02,135
Great, just wonderful.

414
00:19:02,415 --> 00:19:03,735
Can we go film something already?

415
00:19:07,555 --> 00:19:10,255
Rika believes that Senna has a good point, Yozara.

416
00:19:10,515 --> 00:19:13,555
There's no point in worrying about the promises our parents might have made.

417
00:19:13,835 --> 00:19:16,175
What's more important is focusing on the here and now.

418
00:19:16,555 --> 00:19:18,235
So where are we supposed to film today?

419
00:19:19,295 --> 00:19:21,535
I don't know, but let's go make a movie!

420
00:19:26,935 --> 00:19:27,935
Oh, whatever.

421
00:19:28,515 --> 00:19:30,055
I don't even care anymore.

422
00:19:44,055 --> 00:19:45,415
Wait! Big brother!

423
00:19:45,815 --> 00:19:48,115
Hey, Kotaro. What is it?

424
00:19:48,175 --> 00:19:51,395
It's Hirani. He's in trouble, and you've got to help him.

425
00:19:51,475 --> 00:19:51,975
Oh, no!

426
00:19:52,735 --> 00:19:53,955
Fine. Cut.

427
00:19:53,955 --> 00:19:56,815
How do you think it went?

428
00:19:57,435 --> 00:19:57,835
Well...

429
00:19:57,835 --> 00:20:02,955
She's not with us, is she?

430
00:20:03,035 --> 00:20:05,175
We might as well move on to the next scene for now.

431
00:20:08,175 --> 00:20:10,235
Man, I'm so tired.

432
00:20:10,495 --> 00:20:11,175
Huh?

433
00:20:11,175 --> 00:20:18,635
What's up, big bro?

434
00:20:20,835 --> 00:20:22,175
Like you even care.

435
00:20:22,595 --> 00:20:22,915
Huh?

436
00:20:23,255 --> 00:20:26,375
Today was a complete disaster, and it was all thanks to you.

437
00:20:27,375 --> 00:20:28,135
I'm sorry?

438
00:20:28,215 --> 00:20:28,715
I'm sorry.

439
00:20:28,715 --> 00:20:31,895
I can see why you're so upset, and I do apologize.

440
00:20:32,315 --> 00:20:35,655
But you should know we're not the only ones who've heard you and Senna are engaged.

441
00:20:35,655 --> 00:20:38,135
I mean, it's pretty much accepted as a fact at this point.

442
00:20:38,135 --> 00:20:38,335
Who?

443
00:20:38,855 --> 00:20:39,255
Pegasus.

444
00:20:39,475 --> 00:20:41,595
The guy talks about it every chance he gets.

445
00:20:42,255 --> 00:20:45,855
I'd say it's safe to assume that all the faculty and sisters here know about it.

446
00:20:46,315 --> 00:20:48,195
I'd bet some students think it's true, too.

447
00:20:48,715 --> 00:20:51,275
Man, how can just one guy have such a big mouth?

448
00:20:51,695 --> 00:20:53,835
I'm sure he was just excited, Kodaka.

449
00:20:54,475 --> 00:20:55,015
How funny.

450
00:20:55,655 --> 00:20:57,875
So Pegasus was jumping to conclusions.

451
00:20:58,555 --> 00:20:58,955
Huh?

452
00:20:59,155 --> 00:21:00,015
What did you say?

453
00:21:00,155 --> 00:21:01,675
I don't know what you're talking about.

454
00:21:02,335 --> 00:21:04,135
Okay, let's move on to something else.

455
00:21:04,335 --> 00:21:06,115
I heard you guys are making a movie, huh?

456
00:21:06,515 --> 00:21:06,895
Uh-huh.

457
00:21:06,975 --> 00:21:08,275
What kind of movie is it, anyway?

458
00:21:08,515 --> 00:21:11,855
I couldn't make heads or tails out of what Maria was trying to explain to me.

459
00:21:11,895 --> 00:21:12,115
Yeah.

460
00:21:12,455 --> 00:21:13,815
Yeah, I can believe that.

461
00:21:15,495 --> 00:21:16,355
Oh, I see.

462
00:21:16,895 --> 00:21:19,755
So it's a coming-of-age story based on a transfer student.

463
00:21:20,155 --> 00:21:23,775
The more you tell me about it, the more it reminds me of that film Boys Over the Slope.

464
00:21:23,955 --> 00:21:24,235
Really?

465
00:21:24,315 --> 00:21:25,815
I've never even heard of that before.

466
00:21:25,815 --> 00:21:29,815
Yep. It's another coming-of-age movie that most people consider a cult classic.

467
00:21:30,175 --> 00:21:32,055
It's good. I'm surprised you don't know it.

468
00:21:32,535 --> 00:21:34,275
You should watch it for research, at least.

469
00:21:34,675 --> 00:21:37,575
Cool. That sounds like good reference material.

470
00:21:37,975 --> 00:21:38,955
Great idea, Kate.

471
00:21:52,775 --> 00:21:53,815
Wait, Big Brother!

472
00:21:53,815 --> 00:21:55,855
Hey, Godaron, what is it?

473
00:21:56,115 --> 00:21:59,355
It's tyranny. He-he's in trouble, and you've got to help him.

474
00:21:59,935 --> 00:22:01,355
No way.

475
00:22:02,235 --> 00:22:04,135
Yozara, how could she?

476
00:22:04,755 --> 00:22:06,715
Why would she do something like this?

477
00:22:07,235 --> 00:22:09,855
She plagiarized the entire script!

478
00:23:40,877 --> 00:23:42,877
Okay, listen up.

479
00:23:42,877 --> 00:23:44,877
I'll explain exactly what happened.

480
00:23:44,877 --> 00:23:46,877
I thought Senna and Kodaka were dating,

481
00:23:46,877 --> 00:23:48,877
but that apparently was not the case at all.

482
00:23:48,877 --> 00:23:50,877
It may be hard to accept his truth.

483
00:23:50,877 --> 00:23:52,877
I know I can barely believe it myself.

484
00:23:52,877 --> 00:23:54,877
No need to get upset. Let's stay calm.

485
00:23:54,877 --> 00:23:56,877
You seem almost happy about it, Kate.

486
00:23:56,877 --> 00:23:58,877
No, no. I'm not happy in the least.

487
00:23:58,877 --> 00:24:00,877
Next time...

488
00:24:00,877 --> 00:24:03,877
The Sad Case King and the Stone Cold Story.

489
00:24:03,877 --> 00:24:05,877
That Kodaka's got it rough, huh?

490
00:24:05,877 --> 00:24:07,877
Maybe I have a chance with him now.

491
00:24:10,877 --> 00:24:40,117
The Sad Case King's

